<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">contracts</ansi>

Most quests are your own: their experience, gold, items, and skills go
to you alone, and your companions earn nothing from them. A contract is
a quest that hires your whole company.

When you complete a contract, every companion with you earns its company
reward, in full, on top of your own reward: nothing is split, so a bigger
company never shrinks anyone's share. "With you" means alive, still in
your company, and standing in your room when you turn it in, the same as
for experience from a kill. A companion who is away, fallen, or fled
earns nothing, even if they helped along the way, so bring everyone back
before you finish. The quest stays in your own journal
(<ansi fg="command">quests</ansi>), and it pays once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Contracts as the world ships</ansi>

  Rodric's Rats         1000 experience for each companion
  The King's Shadow     15000 experience for each companion

Enough experience is a new level, and the companion's points are dealt
by their archetype (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>). See also
<ansi fg="command">help quests</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.
